1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,610
There are close to 58,000 homeless people in Los Angeles County.
洛杉矶县有近58,000名无家可归者。

2
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:11,770
That’s a shocking and tragic number for a region that’s home to some of the richest people in the world.
对于一个住着一些世界顶级富豪的地区来说，这个数字令人震惊，也令人痛心。

3
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:19,520
At last, the problem became so acute—and so visible—that Los Angeles took extraordinary action.
这个问题终于变得如此严重，也如此显眼，以至于洛杉矶采取了非同寻常的行动。

4
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:27,710
The citizens of this county voted in November 2016 and again in March 2017 to raise their own taxes.
该县公民于2016年11月投票、2017年3月再次投票，决定给自己加税。

5
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:36,540
The purpose of such action is to fund an enormous multibillion-dollar 10-year program of housing and social services for the homeless.
此举的目的是资助一项为期10年、耗资数十亿美元的庞大计划，为无家可归者提供住房和社会服务。

6
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:42,890
As a result, Los Angeles now has its best chance in decades to combat homelessness.
因此，洛杉矶如今迎来了几十年来应对无家可归问题的最好机会。

7
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:47,630
This is an opportunity that surely all can agree must not be wasted.
这个机会绝不能浪费，想必所有人都能认同这一点。

8
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:59,010
It is neither desirable nor morally acceptable nor practical for this county to tolerate the signs of deprivation more commonly associated with the slums of Rio de Janeiro.
该县若容忍那些更常与里约热内卢贫民窟联系在一起的贫困景象，既不可取，在道德上也无法接受，而且不切实际。

9
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,020
How did we get here?
我们是怎么走到这一步的？

10
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:14,520
For as long as there have been homeless people, there has been a tendency to blame the victims themselves for their condition—to see their failure to thrive as an issue of character, of moral weakness, of laziness.
自从有了无家可归者，人们就一直倾向于把他们的处境归咎于这些受害者自己，把他们没能过上好日子看作品格问题，看作道德软弱和懒惰。

11
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:26,440
But contrary to popular belief, the homeless in Los Angeles are not mostly mentally ill or drug addicted or frightening, although a sizable minority meet some of those descriptions.
但与普遍看法相反，洛杉矶的无家可归者大多并没有精神疾病，也不吸毒成瘾，也不吓人，尽管确有为数不少的少数人符合上述某些情况。

12
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:44,490
Today, a greater and greater proportion of people living on the streets are there because of bad luck or a series of mistakes, or because the economy forgot them—they lost a job or were evicted or fled an abusive marriage just as the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving.
如今，露宿街头的人中，有越来越大比例的人落到这一步，是因为运气不好或一连串失误，或者是因为经济把他们遗忘了——他们丢了工作，或被逐出住所，或为摆脱虐待而逃离了婚姻，而恰在此时，住房市场正变得越来越严酷。

13
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:49,820
The challenges are enormous, even if everyone is pulling in the same direction.
即便所有人都劲往一处使，面临的挑战也依然巨大。

14
00:01:50,620 --> 00:02:02,200
That reality was driven home this month by a new Los Angeles Homeless Services Authority report showing that the county’s homeless population is growing faster than the supply of new housing.
本月，洛杉矶无家可归者服务管理局的一份新报告显示，该县无家可归人口的增长速度超过了新住房的供应速度，让人们深刻认识到了这一现实。

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,900
In the world’s richest nation, homelessness on this scale should be shameful and shocking.
在世界上最富有的国家，如此规模的无家可归现象理应令人羞愧和震惊。

16
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:12,810
But most Los Angeles residents are no longer either shocked or shamed.
但大多数洛杉矶居民已不再感到震惊，也不再感到羞愧。

17
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:17,960
Increasingly, we are uncomfortable, annoyed, disgusted, scared or unaware.
我们越来越感到不自在、恼火、厌恶、害怕，或者对此浑然不觉。

18
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,440
Compassion is being replaced by resignation.
同情心正在被听天由命的心态取代。
